// an address only compares against another address. codegen lowers a pointer comparison to an
// icmp over two pointers, and llvm asserts when the operand types differ - so this aborted the
// compiler with "Both operands to ICmp instruction are not of the same type!" and no location.
//
// note this is a different rule from null_compare_value.eco: there the *value* side was wrong,
// here the two sides simply are not the same kind of thing. arithmetic still mixes freely,
// because `$p:$ + 1` offsets an address rather than comparing it
$a = 1;
ptr<int> $p = &$a;
echo ($p:$ == 0);
